@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law s 72 — "תקופת הקצבה", the period of the child allowance. Row IL-08.
-- Source lines 853-856.
--
-- GAPS.md item 6 of row IL-07: row IL-06 answers the allowance on a day, and the capstone asked it
-- about the first day of each month, declining a month in which a child is born or turns 18 after
-- that day. s 72 says which months are paid: from the 1st of the month in which entitlement arose
-- if it arose by the 15th, otherwise from the 1st of the next month; to the last day of the month in
-- which it ceased; only for a child who lived seven days or left the hospital; and for three months
-- after the month in which a child for whom the allowance was paid died.
--
-- WHAT IS ASKED. For one child's entitlement (the day it arose, and how and when it ended), whether
-- the allowance is paid for a given calendar month. Whether a parent is entitled for the child at
-- all, in whose count, and how much, is ss 65-68 (row IL-06).
--
-- THE PERIOD. s 72 carries no amendment tag in the consolidation (line 853), so its text is not
-- dated by an amendment. The row answers months from May 2015, the period row IL-06 answers (its
-- assumption A1), with which these rules compose; an earlier month is declined.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 72 — the period of the allowance`

-- src:853 | סעיף 72 – תקופת הקצבה
-- src:854 | (א) נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 באותו חודש; נוצרה הזכאות אחרי 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 בחודש שלאחריו; תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות.
-- src:855 | (ב) לא תשולם קצבת ילדים אלא בעד ילד שחי שבעה ימים לפחות או שיצא מבית החולים.
-- src:856 | (ג) נפטר ילד שבעדו שולמה קצבת ילדים, ימשיכו בתשלום הקצבה שלושה חודשים מתום החודש שבו נפטר.

-- A calendar month as one count: twelve times the year plus the month less one.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72 — the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` TIMES 12 PLUS `the month` MINUS 1

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d MEANS
    `s 72 — the month count of` (DATE_MONTH d) `of` (DATE_YEAR d)

@ref NII s 72 has no amendment tag; row IL-06 (assumption A1) answers days from 1 May 2015
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, the period row IL-06 answers` MEANS
    REFUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, the period row IL-06 answers"

-- (a), first limb: "עד 15 בחודש" is read as up to and including the 15th (fork N1).
@ref NII s 72(a), line 854
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY (e's `the day the entitlement arose`) AT MOST 15
    THEN `s 72 — the month count of the month of` (e's `the day the entitlement arose`)
    ELSE `s 72 — the month count of the month of` (e's `the day the entitlement arose`) PLUS 1

-- (a), last limb, and (c). NOTHING while the entitlement has not ended.
@ref NII s 72(a), (c), lines 854, 856
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `how it ended`
    WHEN `it has not ended` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` d THEN JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d)
    WHEN `the child died on` d THEN
        IF   e's `a child allowance was paid for the child`
        THEN JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d PLUS 3)     -- (c)
        ELSE JUST (`s 72 — the month count of the month of` d)            -- (a): entitlement ceased on the death

@export Whether the National Insurance Institute pays the child allowance for a child for a given calendar month (from May 2015), under National Insurance Law s 72: from the month entitlement arose (if by the 15th) or the next, to the month it ceased, three months on after a death, and only for a child who lived seven days or left the hospital
@ref NII s 72, lines 853-856
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
          @desc the calendar month, 1 to 12
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
          @desc the calendar year
      e           IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
          @desc the day entitlement for the child arose, how and when it ended, whether the child lived seven days or left the hospital, and whether an allowance was paid for the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for` e MEANS
    IF   `this month` LESS THAN `s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2015
    THEN `this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, the period row IL-06 answers`
    ELSE     e's `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital`                      -- (b)
         AND `this month` AT LEAST `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e
         AND CONSIDER `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e
             WHEN NOTHING   THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST last THEN `this month` AT MOST last
    WHERE `this month` MEANS `s 72 — the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year`
